# questions/pi/extreme 112x32 @0,5 (112x22)
│  ❯ Where stored?  Where should a session's full transcript, every tool result and each compaction summary be
│                   kept once a run ends? Include the archived sessions, the tool_result records and the full
│                   日本語 transcript, not just the latest entry. Assume the developer will often be offline
│                   and needs to carry this between machines without losing any run history.
│
│  ❯ A ○ SQLite in the repository, beside the worktrees        Preview
│        One file the checkout can delete, and no service to   ```sql
│        keep running on any of the machines. Copy it…           create table if not exists event (
│    B ○ Postgres beside the application, shared by every          id integer primary key,
│        machine                                                   session text not null,
│        One more service to run, back up and keep reachable       at text not null,
│        from a laptop that is often offline.                      body json not null
│    C ○ Keep a local log beside each checkout and merge         ) strict;
│        later                                                 ```
│        Works offline without setting up a server, but
│        syncing a single run can produce duplicate records.   A row per event, so the history is the table and
│    D ○ Mirror sessions to an append-only archive as they     a reader can replay it.
│        finish
│        The archive stores every event and preserves links
│        to the original run.
